 "失効日": "تاريخ انهاء الصلاحية (The date on which something runs out or expires and becomes out of date, in many)  [expiry date]",
 "失墜": "ذُلّ (The act of abasing, humbling, or bringing low.)  [abasement]\nمثال: どんな理由があろうと、せっかく軌道に乗せた貿易を失墜させたのは大失態だ。\n→ Whatever the reason, forfeiting the trade that we finally got on track is a fiasco.",
 "失当": "ظُلْم, جَوْر (Absence of justice; unjustice.) / ظُلْم, جَوْر (Violation of the rights of another person or people.)  [injustice]",
 "失意": "خَيْبَة أَمَل (The feeling or state of being disappointed: a feeling of sadness or frustration )  [disappointment]\nمثال: ビルは失意のうちに死んだ。\n→ Bill died a disappointed man.",
 "失感情症": "أَلِكْسِيثَيْمِيَا, لَامُفْرَدَاتِيّة (A deficiency in understanding, processing, or describing emotions.)  [alexithymia]",
 "失態": "خَطَأ (Culpability; the responsibility for a blameworthy event.) / صَدْع, فَالِق (A point at which something is divided, interrupted, or disconnected.)  [fault]\nمثال: あの事件は大統領の失態であった。\n→ That incident was a black mark against the president.",
 "失敗": "فَشَل, قُصُور (State or condition of not meeting a desirable or intended objective, opposite of) / فَشَل (An object, person or endeavour in a state of failure, has failed at something or) / عُطْل (Termination of the ability of an item to perform its required function; breakdow)  [failure]\nمثال: １度や２度の失敗はだれにでもある。\n→ Everybody fails once or twice.",
 "失敗作": "فَشَل, قُصُور (State or condition of not meeting a desirable or intended objective, opposite of) / فَشَل (An object, person or endeavour in a state of failure, has failed at something or) / عُطْل (Termination of the ability of an item to perform its required function; breakdow)  [failure (i.e. an unsuccessful work)]",
 "失敗例": "فَشَل, قُصُور (State or condition of not meeting a desirable or intended objective, opposite of) / فَشَل (An object, person or endeavour in a state of failure, has failed at something or) / عُطْل (Termination of the ability of an item to perform its required function; breakdow)  [(instance of) failure]",
 "失敗者": "خَاسِر (A person who loses; one who fails to win or thrive.) / فَاشِل (A person who is frequently unsuccessful in life.) / فَاشِل (A contemptible or unfashionable person.)  [loser]\nمثال: 一つ間違えると君は失敗者になる。\n→ A single mistake, and you are a failure.",
 "失敬": "عدم احترام (A lack of respect, esteem or courteous behavior.)  [disrespect] / تَرَكَ (To have a consequence or remnant.) / تَرَكَ, غَادَرَ (To depart; to separate from.) / إِجَازَة, عُطْلَة (Permission to be absent; time away from one's work.)  [leaving] / سَرَقَ (To take illegally, or without the owner's permission, something owned by someone) / اِسْتَرَقَ (To move silently or secretly; to pass unnoticed.)  [stealing] / [my apologies ; I must be going now]",
 "失明": "عَمًى (The condition of being blind; unable to see.)  [blindness]\nمثال: 彼はあやうく片目を失明するところだった。\n→ He came close to losing an eye.",
 "失明者": "مَكْفوف  [blind person]",
 "失望": "خَيْبَة أَمَل (The feeling or state of being disappointed: a feeling of sadness or frustration )  [disappointment]\nمثال: 私はその結果に失望した。\n→ I was disappointed at the results.",
 "失格": "إِقْصَاء (The act of disqualifying, or the state of being disqualified)  [disqualification]\nمثال: 彼女は２度のフライングで失格した。\n→ She was disqualified from the race for two false starts. / [being unfit for one's role ; being a failure]",
 "失業": "بِطَالَة, بَطَالَة (The state of having no job; joblessness.)  [unemployment]\nمثال: この地域の失業はほぼないに等しい。\n→ Unemployment in this part of the country is virtually nonexistent. / [losing one's job ; becoming unemployed]\nمثال: 失業した後、彼は大変苦労した。\n→ After losing his job, he went through a very difficult time.",
 "失点": "[lost point (in a game) ; point given away] / [run charged to the pitcher] / أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [mistake]",
 "失着": "أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [mistake]",
 "失礼": "[discourtesy ; impoliteness]\nمثال: あなたはこの前の夜の失礼な振る舞いをスミス夫人に謝罪すべきです。\n→ You should apologize to Mrs. Smith for your rude behavior the other night. / عَفْوًا!, مَاذَا قُلْتَ؟ (An old-fashioned type of dance where partners are constantly changed.)  [excuse me]\nمثال: 「失礼ですが」とアンが話に割って入った。\n→ \"Excuse me,\" Ann broke in. / تَرَكَ (To have a consequence or remnant.) / تَرَكَ, غَادَرَ (To depart; to separate from.) / إِجَازَة, عُطْلَة (Permission to be absent; time away from one's work.)  [to leave]\nمثال: それではそろそろ失礼します。\n→ Well, I must be going. / [to be rude]\nمثال: お返事を書くのがすごく遅くなってしまい、大変失礼いたしました。\n→ I'm extremely embarrassed that it has taken so long to reply.",
 "失礼しました": "أَنَا آسِف, أَنَا آسِفَة (Indicates that the speaker is confused or requests information to be repeated; c)  [I'm sorry]",
 "失礼します": "عَفْوًا!, مَاذَا قُلْتَ؟ (An old-fashioned type of dance where partners are constantly changed.)  [excuse me]",
 "失礼をば": "أَنَا آسِف, أَنَا آسِفَة (Indicates that the speaker is confused or requests information to be repeated; c)  [I'm sorry]",
 "失礼至極": "وَقِح (Not polite; discourteous; not of polished manners; wanting in good manners.)  [impolite]",
 "失神": "إِغْمَاء (The act of fainting, syncope.) / أُغْمِيَ, غُشِيَ (To lose consciousness through a lack of oxygen or nutrients to the brain, usuall)  [fainting]\nمثال: 彼女は失神しそうに見えました。\n→ It seemed as if she was going to faint. / إِغْمَاء (A loss of consciousness when fainting.)  [syncope]",
