 "好奇心猫を殺す": "الْفُضُولُ قَتَلَ الْقِطَّ (One should not be curious about things that can be dangerous.)  [curiosity killed the cat]",
 "好尚": "ذَوْق, طَعْم (One of the sensations produced by the tongue in response to certain chemicals; t) / ذَوْق (A person's implicit set of preferences, especially esthetic, though also culinar) / ذَاقَ, تَذَوَّقَ (To sample the flavor of something orally.) / ذَاقَ, تَذَوَّقَ (To experience.)  [taste]",
 "好意": "إِحْسَان (being kind)  [kindness]\nمثال: リッチ氏は彼女の好意に感謝した。\n→ Mr Rich acknowledged her favor. / حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [liking (for someone)]",
 "好感度": "شَعْبِيَّة (the quality or state of being popular)  [popularity]",
 "好手": "خَبِير, مَاهِر (Extraordinary capable or knowledgeable.) / مُتَخَصِّص, مُتَخَصِّصَة (A person with extensive knowledge or ability in a given subject.)  [expert] / [good move (in shogi, go, etc.) ; clever move]",
 "好景気": "اِزْدِهَار, رَخَاء (The condition of being prosperous: having good fortune and a fortune.)  [(wave of) prosperity]\nمثال: 市の産業はみんな好景気に沸いている。\n→ All the industries in the city are booming.",
 "好材料": "[good material ; valuable data] / بُشْرَى (Something or someone pleasant, fortunate, or otherwise positive.) / بِشَارَة, إِنْجِيل (The message of Jesus concerning the salvation of the faithful, as elaborated in )  [good news]",
 "好機": "فُرْصَة (An opportunity or possibility.)  [chance]\nمثال: この好機を逃すな。\n→ Don't let this chance slip by.",
 "好色": "فَحْشَاء, فِسْق (Inordinate indulgence in sexual activity.)  [lechery]\nمثال: 「好色と倒錯の違いとは？」「好色なら羽を使うが、倒錯なら鶏をまるごと使う」\n→ \"What's the difference between erotic and kinky?\" \"Erotic is when you use a feather and kinky is when you use a whole chicken.\"",
 "好色者": "جاذِبيّة (Shining beauty, splendor, attractiveness or attraction.) / إشْراق, تَهْذِيب (Polish, social refinement.)  [luster]",
 "好評": "شَعْبِيَّة (the quality or state of being popular)  [popularity]\nمثال: その劇は好評を得た。\n→ The play got a favorable notice.",
 "好調": "وَعْد, وَعْدَة (An oath or affirmation; a vow.) / وَعَدَ, تَعَهَّدَ (To commit to (some action or outcome), or to assure (a person) of such commitmen) / بَشَّرَ (To give grounds for expectation, especially of something good.)  [promising]\nمثال: 滑り出しが好調なら事は半ば成就したのに等しい。\n→ Well begun is half done.",
 "好適": "مِثَالِيّ (Optimal; being the best possibility.)  [ideal]",
 "好都合": "مُنَاسِب, مُلَائِم (Serving to reduce a difficulty, or accessible with minimum difficulty; expedient)  [convenient]\nمثال: 天気が暖かくて我々のピクニックに好都合だった。\n→ Warm weather favored our picnic.",
 "好餌": "طُعْم (Any substance, especially food, used in catching fish, or other animals, by allu)  [bait] / مَاصّ (A person or animal that sucks, especially a breast or udder; especially a suckli) / مُغَفَّل (A person who is easily deceived, tricked or persuaded to do something; a naive o)  [sucker]",
 "如": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like...]\nall senses: after が, の, or the attributive form of a verb / [is like... ; is similar to...]\nat sentence end",
 "如き": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like]\nattributive form of ごとし\nمثال: 立て板に水の如きプレゼンテーション、おそれ入りました。\n→ Your presentation was so smooth and fluent - what can I say? / [something like ... ; someone like ...]\nas ...のごときは",
 "如く": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like]\ncontinuative form of ごとし\nمثال: 彼は脱兎のごとく逃げた。\n→ He ran like a scared rabbit.",
 "如し": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like]\nمثال: 過ぎたるはなお及ばざるがごとし。\n→ Too much of a good thing.",
 "如す": "كَـ (having some of the characteristics of (used to form adjectiv)  [-like]\nafter a noun",
 "如上": "الْمَذْكُورُ آنِفًا, السًّابِقُ ذِكْرُهُ (Mentioned or named before; aforesaid.)  [above-mentioned]",
 "如何": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [(depending on) how]\nafter a noun (+ の)\nمثال: 天候のいかんにかかわらず駅へ迎えに参ります。\n→ Rain or shine, I will come to meet you at the station. / [what is ...? ; how is ...?]\nat sentence end",
 "如何こう言う": "تَذَمَّرَ, اِشْتَكَى (To express feelings of pain, dissatisfaction, or resentment.) / شَكَا, اِشْتَكَى (To make a formal accusation or bring a formal charge.)  [to complain]",
 "如何した": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how]\nمثال: 「おぅーい、どうした丹治」「前の学校で習ってない単元があって困っている」\n→ \"Oy, what's up, Tanji?\" \"I'm having trouble because there's a unit I didn't take at my last school.\"",
 "如何せん": "لِلْأَسَف, لِسُوءِ الْحَظِّ (Happening through bad luck, or because of some unfortunate event.)  [unfortunately] / [what can be done about ... ; ... cannot be helped]\nas 〜をいかんせん",
 "如何で": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how]",
 "如何な": "[what kind of ; whatever sort of] / مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]\nمثال: おやおや。いかな体育の授業といえど・・・真剣勝負の意気込みで臨まなければ、いざ実戦と言う時に役に立ちませんよ。\n→ Well, even if it is just P.E. class, if you don't take it seriously, it won't do you any good in a real match.",
 "如何なる": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nمثال: いかなる動物も、植物なしでは生存できない。\n→ No animal can exist without plants. / مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what (kind of)]\nas いかなる...でも, いかなる...も, etc.",
 "如何なる場合でも": "عَلَى أَيِّ حَالٍ (Whatever be the case.)  [in any case]",
 "如何に": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how]\nمثال: 環境汚染にいかに取り組むかは深刻な問題である。\n→ How to deal with environmental pollution is a serious matter. / كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how (much)]\nمثال: 私は教育がいかに重要であるかを痛感しました。\n→ It was brought home to me how important education is. / بِأَيَّةِ طَرِيقَة, عَلَى كُلِّ حَال (In any way that one likes or chooses; in a haphazard or spontaneous way.)  [however (much)]\nas いかに...も\nمثال: 施設は、その使命がいかに崇高なものでも、家庭のかわりにはなり得なかった。\n→ Institutions, however noble their missions, have failed to replace the family. / يَاه, اسمع (An exclamation to get attention.) / هَلَا (An informal greeting, similar to hi.)  [hey]",
 "如何にかかわらず": "بِغَضِّ ٱلنَّظَر عَن, دُونَ الاِهْتِمَام بِـ (Without attention to; without regard for.)  [regardless of]\noften ...の〜",
 "如何にして": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how]\nمثال: 君の成功は主に好機をいかにして上手に利用するかにかかっている。\n→ Your success will largely depend upon how you will make good use of your opportunity.",
 "如何にも": "حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]\nindicating emotive conviction\nمثال: こんな格好をしているといかにもスポーツしてそうに見えるけど、全然やってないんだよ。\n→ I look for all the world like an athlete in this outfit, but the truth is I don't do any sports at all. / جِدًّا (To a great extent or degree.)  [very] / مطلقا, على الإطلاق (In an absolute or unconditional manner; utterly, positively, wholly.)  [absolutely]\nindicating agreement",
 "如何によらず": "بِغَضِّ ٱلنَّظَر عَن, دُونَ الاِهْتِمَام بِـ (Without attention to; without regard for.)  [regardless of]\noften ...の〜",
 "如何に関わらず": "بِغَضِّ ٱلنَّظَر عَن, دُونَ الاِهْتِمَام بِـ (Without attention to; without regard for.)  [regardless of]\noften ...の〜",
 "如何ばかり": "كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much]",
