 "屋": "دُكَّان, مَتْجَر (An establishment that sells goods or services to the public; originally only a p) / تَسَوَّقَ, تَبَضَّعَ (To visit stores or shops to browse or explore merchandise, especially with the i)  [shop]\nusu. 屋\nمثال: 日本にあるインドカレー屋のカレーって、やっぱり日本人の口に合わせて本場よりマイルドに作られてるよね。\n→ The curry they serve in Japan is milder than real Indian curry. They adapt it to Japanese tastes. / [someone who sells (something) or works as (something)]\nusu. 屋, can be derog. / [someone with a (certain) personality trait]\nusu. 屋 / مَجْلِس (A building used for something other than a residence (typically with qualifying )  [house]\nusu. 家",
