 "崩れ": "اِنْهَار (To break apart and fall down suddenly; to cave in.) / اِنْهِيَار (The act of collapsing.)  [collapse]\nمثال: 岩崩れに気をつけて。\n→ Look out for rock slides. / مُتَظَاهِرٌ, طَمُوحٌ (Someone who wishes to be someone or do something, but lacks the qualifications o)  [wannabe]",
 "崩れる": "اِنْهَار (To break apart and fall down suddenly; to cave in.) / اِنْهِيَار (The act of collapsing.)  [to collapse]\nمثال: 本の山は今にも崩れそうに見える。\n→ Those books look as if they're going to topple over any minute. / [to get out of shape ; to lose one's shape]\nمثال: そのバス停で人々は整列して待っていたが、バスが止まるとすぐにその列は崩れた。\n→ At the bus stop, people waited in orderly lines, but as soon as the bus pulled up, the line broke up. / [to break down ; to be thrown into disarray] / حَادِث إِصْطِدَام (An automobile, airplane, or other vehicle accident.) / اِنْهِيَار, اِنْهِيَار نِظَام (A malfunction of computer software or hardware which causes it to shut down or b) / تَحَطَّمَ (To collide with something destructively; to fall or come down violently.)  [to crash (stock market)]",
