 "差し出す": "[to hold out ; to extend (e.g. a hand)]\nمثال: 赤ん坊は小さな手を差し出した。\n→ The baby held out his tiny hand. / حَالِيّ, حَاضِر (Relating to now, for the time being; current.) / مَوْجُود, حَاضِر (Located in the immediate vicinity.) / الزَّمَان, الْحَال (The current moment or period of time.) / قَدَّمَ, طَرَحَ (To bring (someone) into the presence of (a person); to introduce formally.)  [to present] / تَضْحِيَة, قُرْبَان (A human being or an animal, or a physical object or immaterial thing (see etymol) / ضَحَّى ((transitive) to offer (a human being or an animal, or an obj)  [to sacrifice] / أَرْسَلَ, بَعَثَ (To make something (such as an object or message) go from one place to another (o)  [to send]\nمثال: ソフイーは未知の差し出し人からまた手紙が来るのを心待ちにしていた。\n→ Sophie had been looking forward to getting another letter from the unknown sender.",
